    m_UseReference: 1
    m_Action:
      m_Name: Next Button
      m_Type: 0
      m_ExpectedControlType: 
      m_Id: 9e8e768b-5836-43aa-8506-36848a91b8d5
      m_Processors: 
      m_Interactions: 
      m_SingletonActionBindings: []
      m_Flags: 0
    m_Reference: {fileID: -8069514856583376848, guid: 0be0028c24f2a4c14a96b6aa39055933, type: 3}
  dialogueLines:
  - Welcome to H.E.A.T. VR. To learn how to move and interact with the world, please
    proceed by pressing "B" button
  - Let's start with the basics. Your headset tracks your movement. Simply move your
    head to look around you. Look up, down, left, and right. Get a feel for your
    surroundings.
  - To walk, use the Left Thumbstick. Push it forward to move forward, and pull it
    back to move backward. You can also strafe left and right. Go ahead, try walking
    around the area.
  - You can also teleport to move quickly. Push the Right Thumbstick forward. You
    will see an arc. Aim that arc where you want to go. When you are ready, release
    the Right Thumbstick to teleport instantly. Try teleporting to the platform ahead.
  - To turn your view, flick the Right Thumbstick left or right. This will 'snap'
    your view in that direction. This helps prevent motion sickness. Try turning
    around now.
  - To jump, press the 'A' Button on your right controller. Try jumping over this
    small obstacle.
  - To pick up an object, reach out with your hand. When your hand is near an item,
    squeeze the Grip Button on the side of the controller (where your middle finger
    rests) to grab it."
  - Now, try picking up the cube in front of you.
  - To let go of the item, simply release the Grip Button. Go ahead and drop the
    cube.
